From 23a95aaa4bef7148e63bf572f7271a1815e750f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:04:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/pvrsgx: OSSleepms sleeps the milliseconds it is asked for

The services poll for the GPU with OSSleepms(1): for the command queue
to drain, for a free slot in the kernel CCB, and in
ModifyCompleteSyncOpsCallBack for the operations pending on a surface,
which the X server runs into when it touches a buffer the GPU is still
drawing to. OSSleepms was msleep(), which for anything up to 20 ms
sleeps one to two jiffies: 10-20 ms at HZ=100. An strace of the X
server while a page scrolled showed 9 of 97 ioctls taking 9 ms or more.

Use usleep_range() for sleeps up to 20 ms, as timers-howto asks. The
frame rate while scrolling did not change measurably on the N950
(about 21 frames-done interrupts a second before and after).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/env/linux/osfunc.c        | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/env/linux/osfunc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/env/linux/osfunc.c
index 978a1a349..f51d28027 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/env/linux/osfunc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.17.4948957/eurasia_km/services4/srvkm/env/linux/osfunc.c
@@ -792,7 +792,14 @@ IMG_VOID OSWaitus(IMG_UINT32 ui32Timeus)
 
 IMG_VOID OSSleepms(IMG_UINT32 ui32Timems)
 {
-    msleep(ui32Timems);
+    /*
+     * msleep() of a few milliseconds sleeps one to two jiffies, 10-20 ms at
+     * HZ=100. The callers poll for the GPU with OSSleepms(1).
+     */
+    if (ui32Timems <= 20)
+        usleep_range(ui32Timems * 1000, ui32Timems * 1000 + 500);
+    else
+        msleep(ui32Timems);
 }
 
 
